     "dt": 492.898,
     "ev": {
      "type": "result",
      "reply": "Here's your full moving-to-Rouen package, all ready to use. 🎓🇫🇷\n\n**Best neighbourhood: Mont-Saint-Aignan** (where the NEOMA campus actually is). Studios there run €435–560/month on the open market, or €595–645 for a furnished all-in-one private residence (Neoresid, Twenty Campus) — all under your €650 cap. The big win is commute: 5–15 minutes on foot or bike instead of 20–40 minutes by bus from other neighbourhoods <cite url=\"https://neoma-bs.com/about-neoma/campuses/rouen\"/>. One thing to watch: avoid renting right on Place Colbert itself — local press has reported youth-gang disturbances there since 2024 <cite url=\"https://www.paris-normandie.fr/id569558/article/2024-10-17/au-nord-de-rouen-quelles-reponses-linsecurite-qui-inquiete-les-habitants-de\"/>; streets a block or two away are calmer. Rouen Centre (Pasteur) is a good lively runner-up if you don't mind a longer commute.\n\nI had my reviewer check the email and deadlines doc — it caught a couple of real issues, which I fixed: the French email now clarifies \"studio for myself, no flatmates\" and corrects Visale as an Action Logement scheme (not a state guarantee) rather than potentially confusing a landlord; the admin doc now also covers renter's insurance (required before you get your keys) and CVEC (the mandatory student contribution), which I'd missed initially.\n\n**Summary of deliverables:**\n1. **Plan/comparison** — `Rouen-Neighbourhood-Comparison.md`: table comparing Mont-Saint-Aignan, Rouen Centre, and Rive Gauche, with recommendation and search checklist.\n2. **Message** — `Landlord-Email-FR-EN.md`: bilingual (French + English) email to landlords, with subject lines and placeholders for your details.\n3. **Plan** — `Admin-Deadlines-OFII-CAF-Bank-Insurance.md`: OFII (3-month hard deadline), CAF, bank account, health insurance, renter's insurance, and CVEC, each sourced, plus a timeline table.\n4. **Image** — `Move-In-Checklist-Poster.png`: printable 4-stage moving checklist poster.\n\nNo calendar events yet since you don't have exact viewing dates — once you book a flat viewing or get your OFII convocation date, tell me and I'll add real entries to your Google Calendar (I'll confirm with you first). Bonne chance avec la recherche de logement !",
